{"chunk_id": "43f1a764-c5b3-44e6-b010-20076ce81613", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/HowMDVotes.pdf", "title": "HowMDVotes", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 359, "text": "Receive Ballot\n\nAn election worker will\ngive you a ballot.\nTake the ballot to a\nprivacy booth.\n\nMark Ballot\n\nMark the oval to the left of\nyour choice using a black\nballpoint pen. In a general\nelection only, to cast write-in\nvotes, mark the oval next to\nthe write-in space, then print\nthe candidate's name.\n\nReview Ballot\n\nReview that your ballot\nis marked correctly.\nDid you turn it over?\n\nThere may be contests\n\non the other side!\n\n1,2, 35, VOTE\n\nChoose How To Mark Your Ballot\n\nA\n\nA\n\nA\n\nScan the Ballot\n\nInsert Card\n\nInsert the ballot\nactivation card given\nto you by the election\n\nworker.\n\nMake Selections\n\nMake selections by touching the\n\nscreen. Press the “More” button to\n\nsee all candidates in each contest.\nUse the “Previous” and “Next”\n\nbuttons to navigate through the\nballot contests. Or use the key\npad and headphones (or your\n\nown accessibility device) to hear\n\nthe choices and make selections.\n\nReview & Print\n\nReview all selections on the\nsummary screen. Touch a contest to\ngo back and make changes.\nThen touch “Next” to return to the\nsummary screen. Once your choices\nare confirmed press “Print Card” and\nremove the voted ballot. You may\nalso review your printed choices on\nyour printed ballot. Take your\nprinted ballot to the scanning unit.\n\nTE OF MARYLAND\nBALLOT\n\nDEWONSTRAT:\n97/0472816\n861-991. 891-891\n\nOM\nsiete\n‘nuit\nsunita\nCC\nFAVORITE 6\n\nnnn\n\nFAVORITE 0 a\nW/T:COFFEE ©\n\nFAVORITE SEASON- 7\nSPRING\nFAVORITE OLYMPIC SPORTS-----------+\nBASKETBALL\n\n‘SWIMMING\nFAVORITE MUSIC TYPES:\n\nFAVORITE @1ROS-\n\nBALLOT QUESTION 2\n\nBALLOT QUESTION 2---+-\n\nInsert your ballot into the scanning unit.\nYour ballot can be tabulated in any orientation\n(right side up, backward, upside down)\n\n:\n\n:\n\nFavor Birds H\n\n:\n\ni\n\nDee H\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\n:\n\nony :\n\nH\n\nPant H\n\nH\n\n:\n\neon :\n\nSatoanwtont\n\nvr Vote yes or no 1\n\ntok :\ncopeupaniis ne\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\n:\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\nH\n\n:\n\nEnd of Ballot\n\n°)|\n\nA thank you for voting screen will appear after your ballot\nis accepted and dropped into the secure box.\n\nMaryland State Board of Elections elections.maryland.gov #MDvotes vy f\n\nv. 10/2019", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:16:51.610733+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "365ca55b-e3a2-4e7a-8800-ca11a9c18310", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/HowMDVotes_Spanish.pdf", "title": "HowMDVotes Spanish", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 345, "text": "Reciba el voto.\n\nUn trabajador electoral\nle dara un voto.\nLleve el voto a una\ncabina de privacidad.\n\nMarque el voto.\n\nMarque el 6valo de su opciéna\nla izquierda con un boligrafo\nnegro. En una elecci6n general\nsolamente, para emitir votos por\nescrito, marque el 6valo junto al\nespacio para escribir y escriba el\nnombre del candidato.\n\nRevise el voto.\n\nRevise que su voto esté\nmarcado correctamente.\niLo ha dado vuelta?\njPuede haber\nelecciones en\nel otro lado!\n\n> Vole\n\n© Westin\ntga ke\n\n‘© Punch\nPonche\n\nIIe Soda’\nGaseosas\nlo Tea\nTe\n‘© Water\nAgua\n\n‘© or write-info por escrito:\n\nCafé\n\n1,2,3, VOTE\n\nElija como marcar el voto.\n\nal\n\nA\n\nA\n\nEscanee el voto.\n\nInserte el voto en la unidad de escaneo.\n\nInserte la tarjeta.\n\nInserte la tarjeta de\nactivacion de voto que\nle ha dado el\ntrabajador electoral.\n\nRealice las\nselecciones.\n\nHaga selecciones tocando la pantalla.\nToque el botén «Mas» para ver todos\nlos candidatos en cada eleccién.\nUtilice los botones «Anterior» y\n«Siguiente» para navegar a través de\nlas elecciones. O use el teclado y los\nauriculares (0 su propio dispositivo de\naccesibilidad) para escuchar las\nopciones y realizar selecciones..\n\nRevise e imprima.\n\nRevise todas las selecciones en la pantalla\nde resumen. Toque una elecci6n para\nvolver atras y hacer cambios. A\ncontinuaci6n, toque «Siguiente» para\nvolver a la pantalla de resumen. Una vez\nconfirmadas sus elecciones, presione\n«imprimir tarjeta» y retire el voto. También\npuede revisar sus opciones impresas en el\nvoto impreso. Lleve su voto impreso a la\nunidad de escaneo.\n\nSesrstation\n7784/2016\n861-602. 891.\nAnn\nsnvurnuininet\nsuet\nTTY\nCO\nFAVORTTE MARV.\n\nma\nnasa\n\nCHESAPEAKE GAY RETRIEVER\n\nFAVORITE ORINK ceseceseeees\n\nW/T: COFFEE\nFAVORITE SEASON:\n\nSPRING\n\nFAVORITE OLYMPIC SPORTS -\n\nBASKETBALL\n\n‘SUDIOAING\n\nFAVORITE MUSIC TYPES:\n\nFAVORITE 8IROS:\n\nBALLOT QUESTION 2\n\nBALLOT QUESTION 2.\n\nEl voto puede tabularse en cualquier orientaci6n\n(lado derecho hacia arriba, atras, abajo).\n\nUna pantalla de agradecimiento por la votacién aparecera después\nde que el voto se acepte y se coloque en la caja de seguridad.\n\nJunta Electoral del estado de Maryland elections.maryland.gov #MDvotes\n\n= f\n\nv. 10/2019", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:16:57.165325+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "31afc921-6c72-4bf8-ab45-25f549a6ac5a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Mail_In_Ballot_Application-English.pdf", "title": "Mail In Ballot Application English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 284, "text": "Maryland Mail-in Ballot Request Instructions 2025.06 Request a mail-in ballot Any registered voter can use this form to request a mail-in ballot for Maryland elections. Request online Save time and request a ballot online at vote.md.gov/NeedBallot. You will need a MD driver’s license or MVA-issued ID card to use the online form. How do I return Return your completed signed form to your local board of elections. You can return it by this form? mail, fax, email. You can also drop it off in person. Find your local board of elections address at vote.md.gov/LBElist. Make sure to return this form by the correct deadline listed below. How will I receive The primary way to receive your ballot is by mail. my ballot? We can mail your ballot to any address you want. You will also receive a return envelope with prepaid postage. You also have other options. We can email you a link so you can print your ballot, we can fax your ballot, or you can pick it up in person. If you choose to pick up your ballot in person, go to your local election office about 45 days before an election. If you want somebody to pick up your ballot for you, you must provide a Designation of Agent form. Find this form at vote.md.gov/MDagent. When will I receive After you submit this form, we will send your ballot about 30-45 days before the election. my ballot? Deadlines to return this form Your deadline depends on how you return this form and on how you want to receive your ballot. If you mail or hand deliver your request, your form must be in the office before the deadline. Postmarks don’t count.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:16:58.856221+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "2895c092-20a2-4aa4-868d-b309ebfb6a83", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Mail_In_Ballot_Application-English.pdf", "title": "Mail In Ballot Application English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 295, "text": "Deadlines to return this form Your deadline depends on how you return this form and on how you want to receive your ballot. If you mail or hand deliver your request, your form must be in the office before the deadline. Postmarks don’t count. Primary Election General Election To receive your ballot by mail or fax, you must To receive your ballot by mail or fax, you must submit this form by Tuesday, June 16, 2026 submit this form by Tuesday, October 27, 2026 Returning by mail or hand delivery? Submit by 8pm. Returning by mail or hand delivery? Submit by 8pm. Returning by email or fax? Submit by 11:59pm. Returning by email or fax? Submit by 11:59pm. To print your ballot from an emailed link, You To print your ballot from an emailed link, You must submit this form by Friday, June 19, 2026 must submit this form by Friday, October 30, 2026 Returning by mail or hand delivery? Submit by 5pm. Returning by mail or hand delivery? Submit by 5pm. Returning by email or fax? Submit by 11:59pm. Returning by email or fax? Submit by 11:59pm. Track your request status Contact Información en español You can track your Maryland State Board of Elections Si le interesa obtener este formulario request and your ballot at P.O. Box 6486 en español, llame al 800-222-8683. vote.md.gov/search. Annapolis, MD 21401-0486 800-222-8683 800-735-2258 (MD Relay Service) elections.maryland.gov You can ask for this form in large type. Call 800-222-8683. Maryland Mail-in Ballot Request Form To vote by mail, you must be registered to vote in Maryland. Visit vote.md.gov/VoterSvcs to register or update your voter record. Print voter Last name Suffix (Jr., Sr., III, IV, if applicable information 1 First name Middle name or initial Use blue or black ink.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:16:58.856245+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "33665f3e-96b1-4b3d-bf2f-75c6fde8c592", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Mail_In_Ballot_Application-English.pdf", "title": "Mail In Ballot Application English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 279, "text": "Call 800-222-8683. Maryland Mail-in Ballot Request Form To vote by mail, you must be registered to vote in Maryland. Visit vote.md.gov/VoterSvcs to register or update your voter record. Print voter Last name Suffix (Jr., Sr., III, IV, if applicable information 1 First name Middle name or initial Use blue or black ink. Date of birth (mm/dd/yyyy) Residential address This address must match your voter registration so that we can send the correct ballot for your precinct or ward. Provide the address where you 2 Street Unit # are registered to vote. City State MD Zip No P.O. Boxes in this section. Political party Democratic Green affiliation 3 Republican Working Class To vote in a party’s primary, you Unaffiliated (independent of any party) Other: must choose that political party. Election June 23, 2026 Primary Election only You can sign up for a mail-in November 3, 2026 General Election only 4 ballot for upcoming elections or Both the 2026 Primary and General Elections for all future elections. I would like to receive a mail-in ballot for all future federal and state elections Where should we Choose A, B, or C (only choose 1) send your ballot? A Send my ballot by U.S. Mail to If you choose option B, we will Same as residential address in section 2 email you a link to print your ballot about 3 weeks before Or a different address Street Unit # the election. or P.O. Box: City State Zip *If you choose option B or C, we will use the information on your ballot to mark a scannable B Email a link to print my ballot ballot for you. Then we will scan that ballot.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:16:58.856260+00:00"}
