{"chunk_id": "632f3f83-9221-4435-947c-d803a19359bc", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Mail_In_Ballot_Application-Vietnamese.pdf", "title": "Mail In Ballot Application Vietnamese", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 17, "chunk_total": 18, "word_count": 146, "text": "Người trợ giúp, ký tên vào đây (Bắt buộc nếu cử tri được hỗ trợ điền vào biểu mẫu này)\nTAôsis xiisnt acnamt, sđiogann h cehrịue t(Rráecqhu inrhediệ imf t htreư vớoct perh ráepc eluivậetd n hếeul pk hoani tmhias nfo, đrmồn)g thời xác nhận rằng cử tri này cần sự: tUrợn dgeiúr pp eđnể ađltiềyn o vf àpoe rbjiuểruy ,m I ẫhue rneàbyy v cì enrgtưifờyi tkhhaut ytếhti st ậvto hteorặ nc ekehdôendg htheểlp đ wọict/hv itếhti.s C fửo rtmri đ bãe ủcya uqsuey hềne cohr os htôei has\nha odàisna tbhiàlintyh obri ểisu umnẫaub lneà tyo. Nreếaud c oửr t wri rkihteô.n Tgh teh vểo ktýe rv aàou tbhioểrui zmedẫu m neà yto, t côoi mđãp vleiếtet itnh hiso fao trêmn. cIfử t thrie c vũontge rn choưu kldý\nnnhoát ys itgênn tmhiìsn hfo vràmo, đI óp.rinted the voter’s name and wrote my initials.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:33.931906+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ca4577ea-ad85-406e-bb8e-b9ae703685de", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Designation_of_Agent_Form_Mail-In_Ballot_English.pdf", "title": "Designation of Agent Form Mail In Ballot English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 485, "text": "State of Maryland\nMail-In Ballot: Designation of Agent Form\nInstructions: Complete this form if you are not able to return a mail-in ballot application and pick up your mail-in\nballot and would like to designate someone to do this for you. If you are unable to complete or sign this form\nwithout assistance, someone may assist you. The person assisting you must complete Part III: Certification of\nAssistance of this form.\nYou may select any individual to be your agent as long as the person is at least 18 years old and is not a candidate\non your ballot. The individual you name to pick up and deliver the mail-in ballot to you must complete Part II of this\nform and submit this form when your mail-in ballot application is delivered to the local board of elections.\nPart I: This part must be completed by the voter.\nI designate the following person, who is at least 18 years old and not a candidate on my ballot, to act as my agent\nand:\nPlease check the appropriate box:\n□ Deliver my mail-in ballot application, pick up my mail-in ballot, and deliver it to me. I will mail my voted mail-\nin ballot to my local board of elections.\n□ Deliver my mail-in ballot application, pick up my mail-in ballot, deliver it to me, and return my voted mail-in\nballot to my local board of elections.\nName of Agent:\nStreet Address:\nCity: State: Zip:\nPhone Number:\nSignature of Voter Date\nPart II: This part must be completed by the agent.\nUnder penalty of perjury, I hereby certify that I am at least 18 years of age and not a candidate on the voter’s ballot.\nI also certify that I am acting as the voter’s designated agent and will pick up and deliver the mail-in ballot to the\nvoter and if the voter indicated above that I will return the voted mail-in ballot to the local board of elections, deliver\nthe voted ballot to the local board of elections.\nSignature of Agent Date\nIf the agent is returning the ballot, complete this section when the agent returns the voted ballot.\nUnder penalty of perjury, I hereby certify that I am returning to the local board of elections the voted ballot for the\nvoter for whom I am acting as an agent and have not altered the ballot.\nSignature of Agent Date\nPart III: Certification of Assistance. If you need assistance completing this form, the person assisting you must\ncomplete this section.\nUnder penalty of perjury, I hereby certify that the voter named above, who requires assistance because of disability\nor inability to read or write, authorized me to complete this application for him/her. If the voter was unable to sign\nthis application, I have printed the voter’s name on the Signature of Voter line, followed by my initials.\nSignature of Agent Date\nPrinted Name of Assistant\nSBE 9-307", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:35.198554+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "9b3ce3f2-cae7-442d-a726-ff795f6646dc", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/2010_Designation_of_Agent_Form_Spanish.pdf", "title": "2010 Designation of Agent Form Spanish", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 2, "word_count": 285, "text": "Estado de Maryland Papeleta de Votante Ausente: Formulario para Designar un Representante Instrucciones: Complete este formulario si necesita que alguien entregue su aplicación solicitando una papeleta de ausencia y que recoja su papeleta. En este formulario usted puede nombrar a la persona que hará esto por usted. Si necesita ayuda para completar o firmar este formulario alguien lo puede ayudar. La persona que lo ayude tiene que completar la Parte 3: Certificación de Asistencia. Usted puede seleccionar cualquier persona para que sea su representante siempre y cuando esta persona tenga por lo menos 18 años de edad y no sea un candidato en la papeleta. El individuo que nombre para recoger y entregar su papeleta debe de completar la Parte 2 de este formulario y entregarlo cuando el o ella entregue su aplicación para una papeleta de votante ausente en la oficina electoral. Parte 1: Esta parte debe ser completada por el votante. Designo a la siguiente persona, que tiene por lo menos 18 años de edad y no es candidato en mi papeleta como mi representante y que: Por favor marque la caja apropiada: □ Entregue mi aplicación para una papeleta de votante ausente a la oficina electoral local, que recoja mi papeleta y me la entregue. Yo enviaré por correo mi papeleta ya votada a mi oficina electoral local. □ Entregue mi aplicación para una papeleta de votante ausente a la oficina electoral local, que recoja mi papeleta, me la entregue y la regrese ya votada a mi oficina electoral local. Nombre del Representante: Dirección: Ciudad: Estado: Código Postal: N° de Teléfono: (Solamente se usara para procesar esta solicitud.) Firma del Votante Fecha Parte 2: Esta parte debe ser completada por el representante.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:36.304509+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e21f4824-1f9f-42e3-b22b-7d987ff61f08", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/2010_Designation_of_Agent_Form_Spanish.pdf", "title": "2010 Designation of Agent Form Spanish", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 2, "word_count": 291, "text": "Nombre del Representante: Dirección: Ciudad: Estado: Código Postal: N° de Teléfono: (Solamente se usara para procesar esta solicitud.) Firma del Votante Fecha Parte 2: Esta parte debe ser completada por el representante. Bajo pena de perjurio, por lo presente certifico que tengo por lo menos 18 años de edad y que no soy candidato en la papeleta del votante. Certifico además que actuó como el representante designado por el elector y me comprometo a recoger y entregar la papeleta al votante. Si el votante indicó arriba que regresaré la papeleta a la oficina electoral local, yo entregaré la papeleta a la oficina electoral local. Firma del Representante Fecha Si usted también esta regresando la papeleta se le dirá que complete esta sección cuando regrese la papeleta. Bajo pena de perjurio, por la presente certifico que estoy entregando a la oficina electoral local la papeleta votada del votante al cual estoy representando y que no he alterado la papeleta. Firma del Representante Fecha Parte 3: Certificación de Asistencia. Si necesita ayuda para completar este formulario porque tiene una incapacidad o imposibilidad de leer o escribir, la persona que lo ayude tiene que completar esta sección. SBE 9-307 Bajo pena de perjurio, por la presente certifico que el votante cuyo nombre aparece anteriormente, requiere de asistencia debido a su incapacidad o imposibilidad de leer o escribir, me autorizó para que yo completara esta solicitud en su nombre y representación. Si el votante no puede firmar esta aplicación debido a su incapacidad o imposibilidad de leer o escribir, Yo he escrito el nombre del votante en letra de molde en la línea que dice Firma del Votante, y he puesto mis iniciales después. Firma del Representante Fecha Nombre en letra de molde del representante", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:36.304539+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "dc54ba3b-1358-4476-9ebf-f100ebab95c3", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voter_registration/documents/Online Voter Cancellation Form.pdf", "title": "Online Voter Cancellation Form", "section_hierarchy": ["Voter Registration", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 143, "text": "Maryland State Board of Elections “Will\nVoter Registration Cancellation Form\n\nIf you want to cancel your voter registration in Maryland, please complete this form and:\nMail to: Maryland State Board of Elections\nAttn: Voter Registration Division\n\nP.O. Box 6486\nAnnapolis, MD 21401-0486\n\nEmail to: DLVoterRegistration SBE@maryland.gov\nOr Fax to: 410-974-2019\n\nIf you have questions about completing this form, please call 1-800-222-VOTE. Electronic signature is acceptable.\n\nPlease print.\n\nFirst Name: Middle Name:\n\nLast Name: Suffix (if applicable):\nDate of Birth (MM/DD/YYYY):\n\nLast Residential Address in Maryland\n\nStreet Address:\n\nCity: State: MD Zip:\n\nMaryland Driver’s License Number, ID number, Learner’s Permit Number (if known):\n\nLast 4 digits of Social Security Number:\n\nPhone (optional):\n\nEmail (optional):\n\nSignature:\n\nDate of Signature:\n\n151 West Street, Suite 200 « PO Box 6486 Annapolis, MD 21401\nLocal - 410.269.2840 ¢ Toll Free - 800.222.8683 * MD Relay - 800.735.2258\nelections.maryland.gov", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:38.425798+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "fffb2cc2-b9db-489e-bc42-92c4025c3c36", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voter_registration/documents/VRA-English.pdf", "title": "VRA English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voter Registration", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 281, "text": "ie) Maryland Voter Registration There are three ways to register to vote 1. Register online On ao You can also go online to register to vote. Go to: vote.md.gov/VoterApply or scan the QR code apes Zand ot=20}, Mail-in applications available in espanol, francais, Large type Voter Registration Applications are available upon request to your County Board of Elections or State Board of Elections. 2. Mail in a voter registration application What can I use this form for? * To register to vote in federal, state, county, and municipal elections in Maryland. * To change your name, address, or party affiliation. 3. Register to vote during early voting or on election day. Go to an early voting center in the county where you live during early voting, or go to your assigned election day polling place and bring a document that proves where you live. Maryland voter registration form instructions How doI complete this form? 1. Complete Sections 1-8 of the Voter Registration Application, 2. If you need to submit a name change or address change also complete Section 10. 3. Sign and date Section 9. This form must be completed in black ink. How doI submit this form? 1. Tear off this panel at the dotted line 2. Mail your completed application to your County Board of Elections. The mailing addresses are listed on the back panel. * Do not fax or email the form because it requires an original signature. ¢ Submitting the Statewide VRA to an individual other than an official, employee, or agent of a local board does not assure that the form will be filed or filed timely What is the deadline to mail in my application?", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:51.800116+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "a1dfbfb7-562d-497b-bbe2-987a028fc514", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voter_registration/documents/VRA-English.pdf", "title": "VRA English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voter Registration", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 196, "text": "To be eligible to vote in the next election, you must mail your application at least 21 days before election day. What can I expect after I submit my application? If your application is complete and you qualify, you will get a Voter Notification Card in the mail. Do I need to pick a political party? * You only need to choose a party if you want to vote in that party's primary, caucus, or convention. + If you do, check one box only. Confidentiality - Except for items specified as confidential, voter registration records are generally available to the public. : If you decide not to register to vote, that choice stays confidential. This information is only used for voter registration purposes. : If you do register, the name of the office where you turned in your application will stay confidential. Maryland's Safe at Home Address Confidentiality Program can help protect the addresses of survivors of domestic violence and human trafficking. For details, call 1-800-633-9657, ext. 3875. State Board of Elections Confidentiality Program can help protect the contact information of voters at risk in select scenarios. To apply, visit https://elections.maryland.gov/forms/voter.htm| WARNING Am [eligible to vote?", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:51.800157+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "7701a431-f47b-4c5c-9b23-c28397eb7be2", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voter_registration/documents/VRA-English.pdf", "title": "VRA English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voter Registration", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 291, "text": "Maryland's Safe at Home Address Confidentiality Program can help protect the addresses of survivors of domestic violence and human trafficking. For details, call 1-800-633-9657, ext. 3875. State Board of Elections Confidentiality Program can help protect the contact information of voters at risk in select scenarios. To apply, visit https://elections.maryland.gov/forms/voter.htm| WARNING Am [eligible to vote? To register to vote you must be: * aU. citizen + aMaryland resident * at least 16 years old You are not eligible to vote if you: * are under guardianship for mental disability, or if you are, have not been found by a court to be unable to communicate a desire to vote + have been convicted of buying or selling votes * are currently serving a sentence of imprisonment for a felony conviction What information is necessary to confirm I can register to vote? * If you have a current, valid Maryland driver's license, learner's permit or MVA ID card, use that ID number. + Ifyou don't, you must write the last 4 digits of your Social Security number (Election Law 8 3-202). This number is only used for registration and other administrative purposes and will be kept confidential. What if I'm already registered to vote in another county or state? * You must fill out Previous registration information (Section 10) if you are already registered in another Maryland county or in another state. We will then notify the appropriate voter registration agency. Questions? Visit the State Board of Elections website at www.elections. maryland.gov to verify your registration, find your polling place, and find out other important information. If you have any questions, call your County Board of Elections or the State Board of Elections at the numbers listed on the back of the application.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:51.800171+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "f38e0cbe-572f-4411-b9c9-811d1488130a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voter_registration/documents/VRA-English.pdf", "title": "VRA English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voter Registration", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 3, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 284, "text": "Questions? Visit the State Board of Elections website at www.elections. maryland.gov to verify your registration, find your polling place, and find out other important information. If you have any questions, call your County Board of Elections or the State Board of Elections at the numbers listed on the back of the application. Use of your information + This form collects personal information for voter registration purposes. + Ifyou do not provide the required information, you cannot register or vote in Maryland. * You can update your voter registration anytime through your County Board of Elections or by visiting vote.md.gov/Register. * Most voter registration records are public and may be shared with jury commissioners/clerks or other government agencies, as allowed by law. » Voter registration records cannot be used for commercial solicitation purposes. Giving false information on an application for voter registration is perjury, punishable by imprisonment for up to 10 years, and a violation of the election laws, punishable by a fine of up to $1,000, or by imprisonment for up to 5 years, or both. Maryland State Board of Elections SBE Rev 12/25 VRA ‘&) Maryland Voter Registration Form Eligibility Required Reason Required Voter information Required Verification Required Confidential See instructions Residence address Required (No PO boxes) Mailing address If different from your address in section 5. Party affiliation Check one box only. Contact information Signature Required Previous registration information (If applicable) 1 2 1 0 Former address Please compete in BLACK INK. Detach form and fold where indicated to mail. Ifyou answer “No” in response to either of these questions, do not complete this form. Are you a U.S. Citizen? OyYes ONo OYes ONo Check boxes that apply and complete sections 3-9.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:51.800185+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "bdec426e-aed6-444b-9709-63dc255fa826", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voter_registration/documents/VRA-English.pdf", "title": "VRA English", "section_hierarchy": ["Voter Registration", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 4, "chunk_total": 6, "word_count": 300, "text": "Contact information Signature Required Previous registration information (If applicable) 1 2 1 0 Former address Please compete in BLACK INK. Detach form and fold where indicated to mail. Ifyou answer “No” in response to either of these questions, do not complete this form. Are you a U.S. Citizen? OyYes ONo OYes ONo Check boxes that apply and complete sections 3-9. Are you are least 16 years old? _] New registration [_] Name change L] Party affiliation change [_] Address change Last name First name Middle name Suffix Birthdate Month | Day Year Gender ©Male (Not today’s date) OrFemale Ounspecified or Other MD Driver's License (DL) #, . , : Last 4 digits MD Learner's Permit # or of your SSN MD Non-Driver ID # [_]I do not have either a current, valid Maryland driver's license / MVA ID card or a Social Security Number Address where you live Apt or Lot # | City or Town State | Zip Code MD Address where you receive mail Apt or Lot # | City or Town State | Zip Code You must register with a political party if you want to take part in that political party’s primary election, caucus, or convention. Check one box only. If you do not choose a party, you will automatically be registered as unaffiliated. O Democratic © Green © Other — Specify ORepublican © Working Class QUnaffiliated (independent of any party) Email address Phone number I swear or affirm under penalty of perjury that: * TamaUS. citizen. * Tama Maryland resident. * Tam atleast 16 years old. * Ihave not been convicted of buying or selling votes. * Tam not currently serving a prison sentence for a felony conviction. * The information on this application is true to the best of my knowledge, information and belief.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:17:51.800197+00:00"}
