{"chunk_id": "09b17207-62dc-4a65-995d-45a597e5f5de", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 35, "text": ": Round\nOne | Low\nVision: 3 | Blind: 3 | Hearing\nImpaired: 3 | Limited\nDexterity/\nMobility: 7 | Low\nLiteracy: 3 | Mild\nCognitive\nImpairment: 3 | Senior: 2 | Total\nParticipants: 17", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211853+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "bbce1b0f-45d1-4dfc-8ab0-6ef9e45543a6", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 35, "text": ": Round\nTwo | Low\nVision: 5 | Blind: 3 | Hearing\nImpaired: 3 | Limited\nDexterity/\nMobility: 6 | Low\nLiteracy: 0 | Mild\nCognitive\nImpairment: 0 | Senior: 5 | Total\nParticipants: 17", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211871+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "db9cc514-598c-4d99-b297-e6f7b4d0e39d", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 229, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 1. | OBSERVATION: Nearly one-third of our participants (5\nout of 17) relied primarily on the AOL\nbrowser for their Web use. In the next\nelection, this issue could potentially\naffect up to 30,000 voters.\nThis browser is not fully supported for\nthe ballot marking tool. This may be a\nproblem when the ballot marking tool\nis deployed, since many older users and\nother “at-risk” users still use AOL, and\nAOL users are typically less web-savvy\nthan others. Yet these users face mo-\nbility issues that may make the conve-\nnience of absentee voting attractive.\nAdditionally, AOL email does not dis-\nplay links unless users request that links\nbe displayed, which many of the users\ndid not know to do. These users were\nforced to cut and paste the link and\nballot key.\nSeveral users were unable to cut and\npaste successfully. Some users did not\ncapture the full link when copying.\nOne user then pasted the link into the\nsearch bar. | SEVERITY: High | RECOMMENDATION: If voters submit an “@aol.com”\nemail address, send them a spe-\ncial version of the email with their\nballot key that helps them use a\ndifferent browser.\nOr, continue to make the ballot\ncompatible with the AOL browser\n(it got more compatible by the\nend of the week of testing).\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nSENIOR", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211888+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e64ce9ff-eea1-49c0-83ee-8036e3f2e929", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 3, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 89, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 2. | OBSERVATION: One user had great difficultly loading\nthe ballot on his computer since he\nexclusively accesses email through an\niPad, which the ballot does not current-\nly support.\nAs a result he was forced to load his\nemail on his computer, a process with\nwhich he was unfamiliar. | SEVERITY: Low | RECOMMENDATION: Since mobile devices are more ac-\ncessible for some users, consider\nadding mobile support or a mobile\noption in the future.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211896+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "3595f106-3a1c-468a-b36c-62f005d43ac0", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 4, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 119, "text": "None: 3. | OBSERVATION: Inconsistent text regarding the ballot\nacross screens. The user is asked the\nsame question three different ways\nwhich has the potential for confusion:\n• Tell us how you want to download\nyour ballot\n• How would you like to mark your\nballot?\n• Decide how to make your voting\nselections | SEVERITY: Low | RECOMMENDATION: On the “Check your computer”\nscreen, change button text from\n“Next: Tell us how you want to\ndownload your ballot” to\n“NEXT: Choose how to mark your\nballot”\nThe header on the subsequent\npage should be changed from\n\"Decide how to make your voting\nselections\" to\n\"Decide how to mark your ballot\"\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211905+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "c45c5c89-b2b1-4ba7-9866-7ee8777f70cd", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 5, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 57, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 4. | OBSERVATION: Instructions for mailing the ballot only\nappear on the printed ballot form,\nwhich is not accessible for blind or low\nvision users. | SEVERITY: High | RECOMMENDATION: Provide an option for users to hear\nthe mailing instructions if needed.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211912+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "74667abb-820e-4427-aded-87bdea0e384a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 6, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 76, "text": "None: 5. | OBSERVATION: The email describes the ballot access\ncode as a ballot key while the ballot it-\nself describes it as a ballot access code.\nInconsistent language caused some\nusers to paste over the code which had\nalready been passed in. | SEVERITY: Low | RECOMMENDATION: Label both items as a ballot access\ncode.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nLOW VISION\n\nBLIND\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nMILD COGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211918+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "0d51c8aa-29ec-4bdb-a341-1a28b28716a4", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 7, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 71, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 6.. | OBSERVATION: State Question 1 has no subheading; all\nother questions do.\nThese subheadings depend on the way\ndata is entered into the underlying\ndatabase. | SEVERITY: Low | RECOMMENDATION: Continue to work with the data-\nbase team, in order to support the\ninclusion of brief identifying text\nin the navigation panel and review\nscreen for ballot questions.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211925+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "bdf7e073-e845-4fe0-9b41-2d2543e80864", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 8, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 82, "text": "LOCATION: Review | None: 7. | OBSERVATION: When a user re-enters a contest using\nthe \"Click to change\" option from the\nreview screen, the font size used for the\ncandidates name is significantly smaller\nthan the font size on the full ballot. | SEVERITY: Medium | RECOMMENDATION: The very small text works against the\nreadability and usability of the rest of\nthe ballot design. This issue showed\nup after the testing.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nLOW VISION\n\nSENIORS", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211931+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "6c4be72f-32ce-438f-8727-8efaeea876b8", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 9, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 65, "text": "None: 8. | OBSERVATION: IE 8 BUG: When JAWS was reading\nthrough the review screen for each\ncontest, the screen reader read “click to\nbutton” and “change button” as two\nseparate buttons, not as a “click to\nchange button” | SEVERITY: Low | RECOMMENDATION: Work with a JAWS coding expert\nto find a solution.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211937+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "49d6bcd3-8ff6-4b2f-946d-8bc9bb88a59f", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 10, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 105, "text": "LOCATION: Print | None: 9. | OBSERVATION: The ballot PDF is not accessible, which\nmeans there is no way for blind users\nto vote completely independently with\nthis tool. | SEVERITY: High | RECOMMENDATION: Additional explanation for screenread-\ners only may help answer questions\nabout the printed ballot for those who\nrely on screenreaders.\nPossible additions to be read only by\nscreenreader:\n• Instructions for preparing and\nmailing the ballot\n• A courteous explanation about why\nthe PDF is not accessible\n• A reminder that fully accessible vot-\ning will be available in polling places\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nBLIND\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211945+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "ea4371f6-4c1d-4225-aa32-87cbdaac803d", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 11, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 136, "text": "None: 10. | OBSERVATION: Users who looked at the PDF, or at the\npreview page on the print dialog, did\nnot always recognize their ballot.\nOne user exited the PDF thinking it had\nsaved the wrong document.\nThis problem does not exist with users\nwho printed the document successful-\nly because they are able to see all the\npages at once. | SEVERITY: Medium | RECOMMENDATION: The revised first page, with its simpli-\nfied list, was an improvement. Add an\nintroductory title and a MD state logo\nto this page.\nAlso, the documents should print in\nthe order listed on the page (i.e. \"Your\nballot, oath, and other documents will\nbe ready for printing in a moment\")\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nLOW VISION\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY\nSENIOR\nLOW LITERACY\nMILD COGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT\nHEARING IMPAIRED", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211954+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b4545bb6-8259-4f52-8a44-202c409f42f7", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 12, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 127, "text": "LOCATION: Print | None: 11. | OBJECT: On Review Screen, viewing\nNext: Print Ballot Button:\n“I didn’t know I had to print”\n-Participant 8 | OBSERVATION: A handful of users did not know they\nhad to print until the print screen.\nThe mental model of submitting a form\nonline is very strong. Users expect to be\nable to cast the vote as well as mark the\nballot online.\nThe messages about needing to print\nare already very clear. The next step will\nbe clarity in advertising the online ballot\nmarking opportunity. | SEVERITY: Low | RECOMMENDATION: At some point in the future, it will\nreduce dissonance for voters if the\nballot can be submitted as well as\nmarked online.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211962+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e17a1fd3-44b7-48c4-a3c6-df88bb5fc9ea", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 13, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 111, "text": "LOCATION: General\nIssue | None: 12. | OBJECT: (No Image Available) | OBSERVATION: Several issues/bugs with Jaws occurred\nintermittently across browsers. These\nincluded:\n- Jaws not reading drop downs\n- Jaws not reading written information\n(such as name etc) back to user\n- Not reading the status of the check\nbox to the user (i.e. “Checkbox un-\nchecked”), which made one user have\nto guess how to mark the ballot since\nshe was given not instruction | SEVERITY: Medium | RECOMMENDATION: Small code changes sometimes\naffect screen reader function.\nMake sure that the final version is\nthoroughly tested with JAWS.\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211970+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "626349cc-b5d8-42ea-9275-a595e01989b4", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 14, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 61, "text": "None: 13. | OBSERVATION: Some users were unable to print and\nwould have needed to call phone sup-\nport if not for direction from the mod-\nerator. | SEVERITY: Medium | RECOMMENDATION: The phone number for phone\nsupport should be provided on the\npages of the online ballot marking\ntool relating to printing\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211976+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b17f6947-866a-4278-8234-b98f62cd77ad", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 15, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 96, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 1. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: All participants were prompted with a “Only\nsecure content is displayed” notification\nat almost every screen. Unfortunately,\nscreen readers read this notification before\nthe rest of the page, telling the user that\na “notification requires response, press\nAlt+N”. Upon pressing Alt+N, the browser\nskips to the next page before the screen\nreader reads ANY of the content of the\nintroductory pages.\nThe website only displays secure content\nand no longer brings up this message. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: (Notification no longer displays)\nTypes of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211983+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "4ae2d1ee-36c2-463e-b045-7d754b140dfa", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 16, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 46, "text": "None: 2. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Some users finished the ballot, expecting to\nbe able to submit it online.\nA brief explanation about why it cannot be\nsubmitted online was provided. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211988+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e68eb3df-2d42-445d-bb65-e178dcfc2e5d", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 17, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 79, "text": "None: 3. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Header logos and other links were read by\nscreen readers before any page content,\ndistracting and frustrating blind users.\nSocial media icons and SBE logo were\nremoved from the header, header text\nand language options were reorganized in\nthe code of the document, and the “Print\nBallot” and “Log Out” links in the upper\nright corner of the webpage were removed | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.211994+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "9b58c5a9-8633-4fb8-b5cd-92f98e06d98e", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 18, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 76, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 4. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Some users are unaware that they need\nto print the ballot at the time of the vote,\nand only have limited access to printers.\nSimplified introductory text explains why\nballots need to be printed.\nAlso a brief explanation was added about\nwhy the ballot cannot be saved at the\npoint of printing. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212001+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "98f9d1d1-7d59-4906-bbbd-3366e90b903a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 19, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 44, "text": "None: 5. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The word “absentee” is difficult to\nunderstand for low literacy users.\nThe word “absentee” was removed from\nthe text in the log-in pages. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212006+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "4c9e2a22-ab4e-418b-8363-ea2a799500b5", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 20, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 49, "text": "None: 6. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Inactivity time limit was increased to 15\nminutes.\nThe original 5 minute limit was not\nenough time, especially if users needed\nto ask for help or call someone to help\nthem with their ballot. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212011+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "6fb6e906-b8f8-4f73-9e22-07a221ff204d", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 21, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 76, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 7. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The use of the term “agent” (in the context\nof people prohibited from aiding the user\nduring voting) and the word \"template\"\n(refering to the example envelope to be\nprinted if the user cannot print directly on\nan envelope) was unclear to users.\nRephrased: “your employer, or a\nrepresentative of your employer.”\nThe word template was removed. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nLOW LITERACY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212018+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "bdb52607-420a-498b-919f-089e2761cc6a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 22, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 59, "text": "None: 8. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Some users have trouble copying and\npasting the ballot access code from the\nemail.\nUsers are allowed to access their ballot\naccess key by clicking on a link that pastes\ntheir ballot access code for them. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW VISION\n\nBLIND\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212023+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "f0a64e46-b0d7-43e4-9152-801ce2848346", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 23, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 84, "text": "None: 9. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Computer requirements page was stream-\nlined. The problematic “My computer\nmeets the requirements” button was\nreplaced with a “Next” button.\nThe links to browsers led users away from\nthe ballot marking tool and they had trou-\nble finding their way back. Also, the “My\ncomputer meets the requirements” button\ndid not provide a clear call to action; some\nusers did not know how to continue to the\nnext page. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212030+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "4ba7b3a7-dba2-4814-b59d-c52f16ffae14", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 24, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 33, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 10. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Ballot Marking options turned into a\ndrop down menu instead of buttons. A\n\"Next\" button was added to provide a\nconsistent path to the next page.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212035+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "1272b8ff-b528-4df9-8464-47217029ffbb", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 25, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 66, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 11. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Lack of distinction between the two\nBoard of Election contests caused confu-\nsion for users. There was no distinction\nbetween the contests on the navigation\ntabs or in the review screen.\nDistricts were added to inform the users\nthat there are more than one Board of\nElection contest. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212041+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "02518617-1e2f-416a-9252-ecbfd044866e", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 26, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 49, "text": "None: 12. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The text within each contest was made\nlarger.\nLarger text makes the ballot easier to\nsee for low vision users, and may reduce\nor obviate the need for zoom text or\nbrowser zoom. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212046+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b43408ef-fd40-4c48-870e-edf78889734a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 27, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 61, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 13. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Previously the ballot did not alert the\nuser when they had undervoted until the\nreview screen.\nVisual cues were added to the navigation\ntabs on the left hand side to indicate\npartially voted or blank contests. These\ncues proved useful for sighted users. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212052+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "4cd22720-ff13-41dd-983c-7c0a5ce15ea5", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 28, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 74, "text": "None: 14. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The overvoted contest message was\nnot descriptive, was difficult for screen\nreaders to read, and alarmed some par-\nticipants. The prompt name was uninfor-\nmative: “Message from webpage:”\nThe new overvote error message de-\nployed in Round Two is more successful.\nFurther visual refinement of this error\nmessage is in progress. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW VISION\n\nBLIND\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212058+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "89c7d299-d672-4091-b8cd-5511687060e6", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 29, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 85, "text": "None: 15. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Skip to content link did not accurate-\nly skip to content. Those who used\nthis feature still had to listen to or tab\nthrough header links.\nThe code has been altered so the skip to\ncontent link now points to main conent. | ORIGINAL WEBSITE: <div class=”skipNav”>\n<a href=”#primary_content_Block”>\nSkip to Main Content</a></div>\n<div id= “mdgov_globalSiteWrapper”>\n<!--begin primary content area-->\n<a id=”primary_content_Block”\nname=”primary_content_Block” ></a> | ITERATIVE CHANGE: (No image available)\nTypes of Users this will benefit:\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212065+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b3915045-a7dc-4683-a91b-a75f470f8619", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 30, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 63, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 16. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The “Previous”, “Next” and “Review\nBallot and Print” buttons were made\nlarger and the color and spacing changed\nfor added distinction. Also the “Review\nBallot” button changed to “Review and\nprint ballot”. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nMILD COGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT\n\nHEARING IMPAIRED", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212071+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "33fc4074-f773-4478-b4b1-2bb0e4380ed7", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 31, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 68, "text": "None: 17. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The “Write-in Candidate” box can now\naccept punctuation.\nThe previous text box generated an error\nif punctuation was used. For one blind\nuser, the screen reader did not read the\nmessage and she continued to the next\ncontest thinking her vote had been cor-\nrectly recorded when in fact it had been\nerased. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212076+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "507f964c-fd49-4454-9d96-3f5b6a94dfc5", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 32, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 99, "text": "LOCATION: Review | None: 18. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: For ballot measures and questions, the\ninformation on the review ballot screen\nwas too incomplete for participants to\naccurately ensure that their vote was\ncast correctly. Constitutional amend-\nments were only listed by question num-\nber. Without additional text, users were\nnot sure if they had voted correctly.\nThe only way to ensure accuracy in this\nmatter is to re-enter the contest with the\n“click to edit” option.\nSummary information about the ques-\ntions/constitutional amendments was\nadded within the review screen. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212084+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "46b825ca-c55f-4ba7-9b96-959a981dd2e8", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 33, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 96, "text": "None: 19. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Users who inverted webpage colors for\nreadability experienced low contrast on\nthe log-in and review pages. Text boxes\nwere difficult to see and the highlighting\nwhich occurs when a contest is under-\nvoted is difficult to distinguish from fully\nvoted contests.\nNew visual cues added to signal an un-\ndervote were easier to see on an invert-\ned contrast screen; however, this cue\nproved less effective than the previous\none. (See changes from Round Two for\nfinal version.) | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nLOW VISION\n\nSENIOR", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212090+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e280fa5e-6fc2-4d3b-a570-81277d411684", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 34, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 112, "text": "LOCATION: Review | None: 20. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Upon selecting “click to edit” in the\nreview screen, blind participants did not\nknow they had been returned to the bal-\nlot until they had navigated all around\nthe ballot. Furthermore, returning to\nthe review screen was difficult for them.\nThis issue presented as a problem to\nother users as well: “You would think\nthat it would go back to the review bal-\nlot screen instead of the next question.”\n“It’s starting from the beginning?”\n“Click to edit” now returns the user to\na specific contest instead of returning\nthem to the entire ballot. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212098+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "6d5003c7-ef22-48b2-b2f9-7f9ddf7509dc", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 35, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 72, "text": "None: 21. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: On the review page, both low literacy\nand low vision users were reading the\ntext “Click to edit” as “Click to exit”. This\nmade it difficult for these users to figure\nout how to change who they voted for in\na contest.\nThe text “Click to edit” was replaced\nwith “Click to Change”. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212104+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "a68a7475-0c95-440e-b9ba-b4c2d644cc6d", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 36, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 136, "text": "LOCATION: Print | None: 22. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Some users do not have the understand-\ning or printing capability to print an\nenvelope. This was a challenge for older\nusers with limited problem-solving skills,\nand users with low vision, low dexterity,\nand blindness, who may not be able to\ncopy an address from the instructions\nonto a blank envelope.\nAlso, the page headline text on this\nscreen reads “choose your envelope\ntype,” which is misleading because no\nchoice is given. You only choose if you\ncan or cannot print an envelope.\nText was changed on the intro screen\nto say: “You must print and MAIL your\nballot and envelope”.\nThe intro screen also includes a brief\nexplanation about why ballots are not\nsaved or submitted electronically. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212112+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "f6b6e569-3940-4961-b6e6-9c6921d8b6de", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 37, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 25, "text": "None: 23. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: “Print Envelope” is now a button instead\nof a link. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212116+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "1a2154ce-abf0-4b2f-afa9-0fcd3098ea48", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 38, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 45, "text": "LOCATION: Print | None: 24. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The printing order of the ballot and\nenvelope has been switched to better\nfit the user’s mental model. The ballot\nnow prints first instead of the envelope. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212122+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "5841a517-9464-471c-8aa0-17e4091ebb28", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 39, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 60, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 1. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Some users did not find the buttons to\nmove forward to the next screen.\nChanges to buttons improved their click\nrate:\n-Buttons were made much larger\n-Colons, capitalization, and additional\ninformation were added to buttons (i.e.\nNext: Print Envelopes)\n-Punctuation was removed | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212127+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "2f1499d5-1b9b-4048-bda7-250aa7460a71", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 40, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 47, "text": "None: 2. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The page about getting assistance was\nnot working well with screenreaders.\nThe new page, with simple buttons,\nworks well with screenreaders and\nprovides a simpler, cleaner interaction.\nEliminating the dropdown increases\naccessibility. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212132+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "1299db70-f327-4fe7-915c-cd8e00edd12b", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 41, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 64, "text": "None: 3. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Change to the computer requirements\npage:\nOld text: “A recent version of your\nfavorite Web Browser. If you use internet\nexplorer, it must be at least version 9.”\nNew text: “An up-to-date version of\na supported Web Browser: Firefox,\nChrome, Safari, Opera, or Internet\nExplorer.” | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY\nLOW LITERACY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212138+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "6e148991-de48-4d86-8454-4f44fa96316e", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 42, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 117, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 4. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The instructions located under the Ballot\nAccess Code entry went through sever-\nal iterations which continued to cause\nconfusion for users. At one point the\ninstructions directed the user to copy and\npaste the ballot code from the email they\nreceived, even though sometimes this field\nwas pre-populated. This caused users to\ndelete the code already present and return\nto the email and copy and paste the code\nin.\nNow the directions under the ballot access\ncode read, “If this is blank, copy and paste\nthe ballot access code from the email you\nreceived from the Board of Elections.” | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212145+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "684b9feb-61bd-4d88-b6d8-979eb95c95f8", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 43, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 137, "text": "None: 5. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The dropdown menu was difficult to use\nfor some users with ZoomText/screen\nmagnification as it would deploy up in-\nstead of down, causing users these users\nto miss the drop down options. The drop\ndown is also a hassle for blind users who\nneed the screen reader to read each year\nto them.\nDrop down menus were also difficult to\nclick for users with limited manual dexter-\nity. Users struggled with the small size of\nthe arrows and moving their mouse to just\nthe right part of the scroll button.\nTo increase ease of use and reduce the\ntime to log-in for blind users, the birth\ndate dropdown boxes were replaced with\ntext boxes so users can manually enter\ntheir birth date. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212157+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "9a84ba6d-85d7-4b98-8766-1ee58be8728b", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 44, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 130, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 6. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Users were unclear as to the level of assis-\ntance required to check yes on the “Tell us\nif someone is helping you” page.\nOne blind user asked “If they show me\nwhere the line is, is that helping me sign?”\nAnother blind user stated “I have to mark\nyes because I’m not sure how the signing of\nthe ballot is going to work.”\nAn additional line of text was added to alert\nusers what is involved in the ballot marking\nprocess, the text now reads, “This system\nrequires that you print your ballot, sign an\noath, and mail both.” | ITERATIVE CHANGE: *Solution not yet confirmed by testing.\nTypes of Users benefited from change:\n\nLIMITED DEXTERITY\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212165+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "33944807-fa09-4813-bc57-7f4f1407caef", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 45, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 131, "text": "None: 7. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Users did not recognize that the \"Next\nmake sure your computer meets the re-\nquirements\" button on the initial login page\nbutton was clickable. Users searched for\nhow to proceed, and did not know how to\nmove forward. Once users were prompted\nto click the button, they figured the rest of\nthe pages out easily.\nBlind users relying on screen readers also\nskipped over this link thinking there would\nbe additional text or information about\ncomputer requirements below.\nMaking this button larger, and refining the\ntext helped, but further improvements may\nbe necessary.\nThe cursor now turns into a \"hand\" when\nthe user mouses over the button. This\nshould help. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users this will benefit:\n\nSENIOR\n\nCOGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT\n\nLOW LITERACY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212173+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e3676b2e-8f96-4435-9f9c-5d50060ed34a", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 46, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 146, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 8. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: In the log-in page, one user had trouble\nlogging in due to a suffix on his name.\nA more robust error message was added\nfor when the voter’s name is not found.\nIt reads as follows:\n“That voter and ballot key combination\nis not valid. Before trying again, please\ncheck the following:\n1) Enter your name the same way your\nregistered to vote. For example, if you\nregistered to vote as ‘Jeff’ instead of\n‘Jeffrey, use ‘Jeff’ for the search.\n2) Do not include a suffix such as Jr. or Sr.\nin the last name field.\n3) If you changed your name recently,\nenter your former name.\n4) If you moved recently, enter the zip\ncode where you lived before.” | ITERATIVE CHANGE: *Change not yet functional at time of\nreport\nTypes of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212181+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "47abcb2e-b349-4622-bb5e-86f8566e4765", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 47, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 74, "text": "None: 9. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The options of “You can use your com-\nputer to vote your ballot OR Print a\nblank ballot and mark by hand” makes\nit seem as if there is an option to vote\nentirely online.\nOptions now read “You can use your\ncomputer to mark and print your bal-\nlot OR Print a blank ballot and mark by\nhand” | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212187+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "c0f60b14-ed88-4543-8ad5-c78985941400", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 48, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 136, "text": "LOCATION: Login | None: 10. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Many users clicked the link that accesses\nthe ballot and passes in the key without\nrealizing that the code is automatically\nput into the ballot. This may be because\nusers do not know what “pass in your\ncode” means. As a result some users\nwould go back and cut and paste the\nballot access code from their email, even\nthough the ballot access code field was\npre-filled.\nThe text in the email was simplified to\nread as follows:\n\"Access your ballot now.\nIf the link above does not work for you:\n1. Copy and paste the following link\ninto your browser:\nhttps://voterservices.elections.state.\nmd.us/ballot_wizard_redesign\n2. Copy the following BALLOT KEY\nwhen prompted.\n8ee1cda3-10c5-4451-82a3-\nf071772ee9d6\" | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users this will benefit:\n\nLOW VISION\n\nBLIND\n\nSENIOR", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212196+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "164909f6-a3b6-4895-b3ad-67526af449b4", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 49, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 63, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 11. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The write-in process had bugs that im-\npacted use, and was not easy to use with\nscreenreaders.\nSolution: The write-in process was made\nan out-and-back interaction with its own\nscreen. This version worked well with\nscreen readers. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW VISION\n\nBLIND\n\nLOW LITERACY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212202+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "0cef8050-2977-4f0e-852a-85f75ffd8d32", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 50, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 94, "text": "None: 12. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: There was no mention in the email or on\nthe site about whether mobile devices\ncan be supported, causing one user to\ntry and retrieve the ballot on his iPad.\nThe following text was added to one of\nthe initial log-in screens to indicate that\nmobile devices are not currently sup-\nported: “Note: this system has not yet\nbeen tested on mobile devices. It may or\nmay not work for your mobile device.” | ORIGINAL WEBSITE: (no image available) | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212209+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "008dfb3d-647b-4dd1-862f-8bbfa80c819e", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 51, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 203, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 13. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The title of the overvote error message\nwas unhelpful (“the page at http://vot-\nerservices.elections.state.md.us says”),\nwhich caused it to look like a general\nbrowser error, and was not fully read by\nall participants.\nAlso, one ZoomText user could not even\nsee the error message since the position\nof the message defaults to the middle\nof the page, which was not in the user’s\nfield of view at the time. After over-\nvoting, he attempted to navigate to the\nnext contest using the side navigation\ntabs but could not proceed, and he did\nnot know why. He had no idea that\nthere was an error message present that\nrequired his attention to proceed.\nThe new overvote error message has a\nmore helpful title (“Maximum selections\nmade.”). Additionally, the error box was\nformatted with a bright stroke around\nthe entire edge so as to create a stronger\nvisual cue for users with screen magnifi-\ncation or ZoomText, who may only have\nthe edge of the error message in their\nvisual field.\nFurther visual refinement of this error\nmessage is in progress. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW VISION\n\nLOW LITERACY", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212220+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "3e0f53b8-434e-4c6f-b64c-6217803b5ebc", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 52, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 100, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 14. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: A few users relied on the side navigation\nbar in order to progress through the bal-\nlot, yet they had no way to review their\nballot from this menu. This was a sig-\nnificant problem for one ZoomText user\nwho relied exclusively on the side nav-\nigation and could not see the “Review\nand print ballot” button located under\nthe contest due to her limited field of\nvision.\nA blue “Review and Print Ballot” button\nwas added to the side navigation bar. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212227+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "5aae5dcb-ae53-4919-8fdd-20ba0c5b15e1", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 53, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 77, "text": "None: 15. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: When users reach the end of the ballot,\nthey no longer reach a blank screen that\nhas the buttons “Previous” “Next” and\n“Review and Print Ballot”.\nNow they see the last contest, with only\nthe “Previous” and “Review and Print\nBallot” buttons available.\n*Though this issue was resolved in a\nprevious iteration, it has since re-\noccured and is currently being resolved. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212234+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "b6626396-9422-467c-a80e-9a8be35764b5", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 54, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 83, "text": "LOCATION: Ballot | None: 16. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Some users hesitated when figuring out\nwhich button to choose after writing in\ntheir ballot selection.\nThe three buttons were made to be the\nsame width, so that the “Save and Close”\nbutton has equal weight with the others.\nThis solution has not yet been con-\nfirmed by testing. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users this will benefit:\n\nLOW VISION\n\nIMPAIRED MOBILITY\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW LITERACY\n\nMILD COGNITIVE IMPAIRMENT\n\nHEARING IMPAIRED", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212240+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "06253bb8-89ba-457d-98c3-fbb17cbd2e68", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 55, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 74, "text": "LOCATION: Review | None: 17. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The updated visual cue for undervoted\ncontests was not strong enough for users\nto easily detect. Many users missed un-\ndervoted or partially voted contests.\nAdditional visual cues were added to\nshow that a contest is undervoted. The\nvisual cue was deigned to be strongly\nvisible, even when the screen contrast is\ninverted. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212246+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e8cd2f86-73a6-44c4-b74a-067dd6180010", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 56, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 77, "text": "LOCATION: Print | None: 18. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Many users do not proceed to the log\nout page, especially those who know\nthey cannot print an envelope, as they\nsee no reason to continue to the next\npage.\nButton text on the “Your Ballot is Printing\nPage” has been revised to say “Print En-\nvelope or log-out” and a log-out button\nwas created on the subsequent page. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212251+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "0f046103-daa0-47cb-9095-0a468a611bb1", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 57, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 77, "text": "None: 19. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: The print dialog is very slow to appear\nand for some the print dialog never\nappears at all. This creates problems as\nusers search for additional options to\nprint.\nThe text that was added to this screen\n(“Your ballot, oath, and other documents\nwill be ready for printing in a moment”)\nhelped users.\nOption to download PDF and reprint was\nalso helpful. | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212257+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "892602f6-b566-4506-9ace-bb0100174105", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 58, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 61, "text": "LOCATION: Print | None: 20. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Users had trouble finding key informa-\ntion in the ballot instructions. A simpli-\nfied ballot checklist was added to begin-\nning of the printed ballot packet\nFurther improvements will make this\nballot checklist easier to identify as part\nof the MD ballot package | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nALL", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212263+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "87025fc9-e690-4375-ab0d-e9e62de253c3", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 59, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 90, "text": "None: 21. | OBSERVATION/RECOMMENDATION: Not all users were finding the link to\n“download the pdf now” if their ballot\ndid not print.\nThe new link starts on a new line, and\nprovides more information. The text\nabout what documents are printing was\nalso improved:\nOld text: “You should have printed a doc-\nument containing your ballot and other\nimportant documents”\nNew text: “Your ballot, oath, and other\ndocuments will be ready for printing in a\nmoment.” | ITERATIVE CHANGE: Types of Users benefited from change:\n\nSENIOR\n\nLOW VISION", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212269+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "90a47270-ff06-4eff-8332-7ffd4f7786dc", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/press_room/documents/OnlineBallot_UsabilityTestResults.pdf", "title": "OnlineBallot UsabilityTestResults", "section_hierarchy": ["Press Room", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 60, "chunk_total": 94, "word_count": 26, "text": "Participant\n#: p1 | Age: 52 | Gender: Male | Race/\nEthnicity: African American | Factors Affecting\nComputer Use: Low Literacy | Assistive\nTechnology Used: None", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:23:24.212274+00:00"}
