{"chunk_id": "95126b29-5c21-44cb-847d-9170f4ff27f3", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Rules for Observing Canvasses_10152024.pdf", "title": "Rules for Observing Canvasses 10152024", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 200, "text": "KX,\nMaryland State Board of Elections ce)\nRules of Conduct for Canvass Observers \\ge@\n\nMembers of the public and media are encouraged to observe the local board of\nCanvassers canvass mail-in and provisional ballots. During the canvasses, it is the\nresponsibility of the local board of canvassers to maintain order and safeguard all\nrecords and documents. Please be mindful of the following rules of conduct for\nindividuals observing a canvass.\n\nPrint your name on the canvass sign-in sheet\nDirect all questions to the Election Director or his or her designee\n\nYou may observe the canvass teams reviewing the ballots but must maintain a\nreasonable distance\n\nDo not touch the ballots or other election documents\nDo not make excessive noises or cause distractions\nNo food or drink are allowed in the canvassing room\nDo not use cell phones or other audible devices in the canvassing room\n\nTaking pictures and recording a canvass is permitted as long as it does not\n\ndisrupt the canvass or interfere with other people attending and observing the\ncanvass\n\nIf you have information that you believe should be considered by the Board of\nCanvassers, immediately notify the Election Director or his or her designee\n\nCOMAR 33.08.03.05(C)(1) 10/24", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:02.327828+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "eb3b1ac8-7ba6-47ae-a975-25362d525616", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/voting/documents/Canvass Challenge Form_10112024.pdf", "title": "Canvass Challenge Form 10112024", "section_hierarchy": ["Voting", "Documents"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 1, "word_count": 252, "text": "<\n\n. *\n\nMaryland State Board of Elections~*,\n\nCanvass Challenge Form\n\nInstructions: State regulations permit an individual to challenge an action of a local Board of Canvassers. If you\nwish to challenge a decision to accept or reject a mail-in or provisional ballot, notify the election director or his or\n\nher designee, complete this form, and return it to the election director or his or her designee. You may only\nchallenge a decision during the canvass at which the ballot was accepted or rejected.\n\nOnce you submit this completed form, the ballot(s) being challenged and related documents (oath and envelope if\na mail-in ballot or provisional ballot application if a provisional ballot) will be put aside for consideration by the local\nBoard of Canvassers. The local Board will review the information on this form to decide whether to change its\n\ndecision to accept or reject the ballot(s) in question. All challenged ballots will be separated from other ballots. If\nthe local Board affirms its acceptance of the ballot(s), the ballot(s) will be counted on a separate memory card.\n\nDate\nPart 1 — Completed by challenger\n\n© Challenge of mail-in ballot(s) © Challenge of provisional ballot(s)\n\nName of Organization (if applicable)\n\nLast Name First Middle\nStreet Address_ sé pt.\nCity State Zip\nPhone Number Email address\n\nNumber or description of ballots being challenged:\n\nReason for Challenge\n\nSignature\n\nPart 2 —- Completed by election director or designee Challenge #\n\nNumber of challenged ballots\nNumber of challenged ballots accepted Number of challenged ballots rejected\n\nComments", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:04.529379+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "f6f2407b-6be7-44ec-8d99-1cdadfac7430", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/Challenger_and_Watchers_Manual.pdf", "title": "Challenger and Watchers Manual", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 28, "word_count": 32, "text": "In addition to the prohibited activities listed under #12(b), you cannot use cameras and electronic: devices, such as phones, smart watches, laptops, and tablets, in the polling place. You must be outside", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:09.191169+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "f3b148be-57a3-4856-aead-516d48f892d0", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/Challenger_and_Watchers_Manual.pdf", "title": "Challenger and Watchers Manual", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 28, "word_count": 33, "text": "In addition to the prohibited activities listed under #12(b), you cannot use cameras and electronic: the polling place and the “no electioneering” zone to use any electronic device. You cannot act as voter", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:09.191184+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "55772b82-8918-42fc-8809-17b48e92b8e7", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/Challenger_and_Watchers_Manual.pdf", "title": "Challenger and Watchers Manual", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_total": 28, "word_count": 34, "text": "In addition to the prohibited activities listed under #12(b), you cannot use cameras and electronic: advocates or attempt to exercise political influence while in the polling place. This is not the role of a", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:09.191190+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "961846eb-0e56-4d9f-ac6d-4d9e791d636e", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/Challenger_and_Watchers_Manual.pdf", "title": "Challenger and Watchers Manual", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 3, "chunk_total": 28, "word_count": 31, "text": "In addition to the prohibited activities listed under #12(b), you cannot use cameras and electronic: challenger or watcher, and if you do this, you will be removed from the polling place.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:24:09.191196+00:00"}
