{"chunk_id": "a6878a1c-2243-410b-8d2c-148dcdb97d73", "source_url": "https://elections.maryland.gov/pdf/summary_guide/coo.pdf", "title": "coo", "section_hierarchy": ["Pdf", "Summary Guide"], "page_classification": "document", "chunking_strategy": "document_extraction", "chunk_index": 2, "chunk_total": 28, "word_count": 125, "text": ": In accordance with §13-207(d)(1) of the Election Law Article, Annotated Code of Maryland, I hereby resign as Chairman. And, I\nhereby certify that I have returned all records relating to the campaign finance entity to the remaining officer or the candidate and I have\ncompleted all of my campaign finance reporting responsibilities.*\n_______________________________________________________ __________________________________________________\nSignature of Resigning Officer Date Printed Name of Resigning Officer\n*Depending on when you file your resignation, you may remain liable for the next Campaign Finance Report. Call the State Board of Elections to clarify your reporting\nresponsibilities. In addition, it is recommended that you file a statement with your resignation reporting your committee or entity’s cash balance, the amount of money in\nthe checking account, and any outstanding obligations.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T16:25:25.103554+00:00"}
