{"chunk_id": "ab628539-0d41-476b-bad2-e0af41af4183", "source_url": "local://2026-01/Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1.pdf", "title": "Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-01"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 3, "chunk_total": 47, "word_count": 275, "text": "Turnout Estimate Site is of sufficient size to handle voter traffic. Site Agreement Signed and submitted ADA Survey Site is ADA compliant . Signal Strength Survey Submitted for review. Security Plan Submitted for review. F r e d e r i c k BALLOT DROP BOXES: THE OVERVIEW NOTES: Same number of boxes as 2024 1 box relocated LOCATIONS: Drop Box Location Address Brunswick Middle School 301 Cummings Drive, Brunswick, MD 21716 Crestwood Middle School 7100 Foxcroft Drive, Frederick, MD 21703 Frederick County Board of Elections Office 8490 Progress Drive, Federick, MD 21701 Trinity Recreation Center (replaces Frederick 6040 New Design Road Frederick 21703 Prospect Center, 585 Himes Avenue, Frederick, MD 21703) Middletown VFD Activities Building 1 Fireman's Lane, Middletown, Md 21769 Oakdale High School 5850 Eaglehead Drive, Ijamsville, MD 21754 Thurmont Regional Library 76 E. Moser Road, Thurmont, MD 21788 Urbana Regional Library 9020 Amelung Street, Frederick, MD 21704 Waverley Elementary School 201 Waverley Drive, Frederick, MD 21702 William R. Talley Recreation Center 121 N. Bentz Street, Frederick, MD 21701 Libertytown VFD Activities Hall 12027 South Street, Libertytown 21762 Wolfsville Elementary School 12520 Wolfsville Road, Myersville 21773 F r e d e r i c k POLLING PLACE PLANS: THE OVERVIEW Building, Precinct, and Polling Places comparison 2022 to 2026 2022 2024 2026 Number of 58 54 54 Individual Buildings Number of 83 66 66 Precincts Number of 63 56 56 Polling Places Frederick County - Historically Disenfranchised Community Analysis LBE provided the required analysis of the impact on the ability of historically disen