{"chunk_id": "9526ce01-8dfe-4124-8967-be2d5ad8e449", "source_url": "local://2026-01/Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1.pdf", "title": "Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-01"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 7, "chunk_total": 47, "word_count": 280, "text": "YELLOW SPRINGS 8717 YELLOW No suitable facility 21003 No 21-001 N ELEM SCH SPRINGS RD available. WHITTIER ELEM 21008 2400 WHITTIER DR No 21-002 SCHOOL BROOK HILL UNITED 8946 INDIAN No suitable facility 21009 No 21-001 N METHODIST SPRINGS RD available. CHURCH ORCHARD GROVE 5898 HANNOVER No suitable facility 23001 No 23-005 N ELEM SCHOOL DR available. ORCHARD GROVE 5898 HANNOVER No suitable facility 23002 No 23-005 N ELEM SCHOOL DR available. 2018 location (Grace Community Church) no longer available. Absorbing 24-004/005/006 due to identical ballot style. 2022 location (People's Baptist Church) experienced WAVERLY ELEM 201 WAVERLEY 24002 No 02-008 Y voter confusion due SCHOOL A DRIVE to difficulty finding the church location, and complaints due to lack of year-round climate control. Location is unsuitable as it has no air conditioning and minimal heating. WALKERSVILLE 81 WEST No suitable facility 26002 No 26-001 N HIGH SCHOOL FREDERICK ST available. Frederick County - Polling Places Used in 2022 but Not in 2026 BUILDING IN JUSTIFICATION SUITABLE FOR LOCATION USED PRECINCT WITH POLLING PLACE ADDRESS FOR NOT USING PRECINCT USE IN 2024 NO POLLING LOCATION IN 2026 PLACE Voter confusion in previous years due to People's Baptist Church difficulty finding the (in 2022, previously 6648 Carpenter Road, No NO church location, and 24002 NO Grace Community Frederick 21703 complaints due to lack Church in 2018) of year-round climate control. In 2024 03-001 and 03-003 were consolidated, eliminating 03-003 due 100 Martha Mason Middletown Middle to identical ballot style. Street, Middletown NO NO 3001 NO School Moving 03-001 to 21769 Middletown Primary School places polling place within precinct boundary. In 2024 09-006 and 09-008 were consolidated, eliminating 09-008 due to identical ballot style.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:03.515799+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "e67166f1-9016-47c8-8940-a4968b5d3814", "source_url": "local://2026-01/Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1.pdf", "title": "Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-01"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 8, "chunk_total": 47, "word_count": 282, "text": "In 2024 03-001 and 03-003 were consolidated, eliminating 03-003 due 100 Martha Mason Middletown Middle to identical ballot style. Street, Middletown NO NO 3001 NO School Moving 03-001 to 21769 Middletown Primary School places polling place within precinct boundary. In 2024 09-006 and 09-008 were consolidated, eliminating 09-008 due to identical ballot style. Oakdale Elementary 5830 Oakdale School NO NO Moving 09-006 to 9008 NO School Road, Ijamsville 21754 Spring Ridge Elementary School places polling place within precinct boundary. In 2024 14-001 and 14-002 were Valley Elementary 3519 Jefferson Pike, NO NO consolidated, 14001 NO School Jefferson 21755 eliminating 14-002 due to identical ballot style. In 2024 24-001 and 6909 Maryland 24-003 were Church of Avenue, Frederick NO NO consolidated, 24001 NO Transfiguration 21703 eliminating 24-003 due to identical ballot style. Twin Ridge Elementary School, the usual polling location for Precinct 18-01, will be undergoing significant construction projects during the period of the Primary Election. The construction would compromise voter safety, accessibility, and the ability to set up a fully functional and 1106 Leafy Hollow ADA compliant polling Twin Ridge Elementary Circle, Mount Airy No Yes place that meets state 18-01 Yes School 21771 standards. Precinct 18-01 voters will report to Kemptown Elementary School for the June 23 Primary Election only. Precinct 09-04 votes at Kemptown Elementary School (operating from the Cafeteria); however, Precinct 18-01 will be set up in a separate room within the school. Ample signage and election staff will be on site to guide voters to the appropriate check-in area for their precinct. The regularly scheduled polling place for Precinct 18-02, Damascus Road Community Church, will be unable to host voting operations on the date of the Primary Election.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:03.515809+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "db2a0aff-fbdb-45e1-85dd-fa4aa5ecd0ff", "source_url": "local://2026-01/Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1.pdf", "title": "Election Plan Board Presentation Part 1", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-01"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 9, "chunk_total": 47, "word_count": 286, "text": "Ample signage and election staff will be on site to guide voters to the appropriate check-in area for their precinct. The regularly scheduled polling place for Precinct 18-02, Damascus Road Community Church, will be unable to host voting operations on the date of the Primary Election. The church is beginning a school program that will be in session and fully occupying the facility throughout the entire day on June 23, 12826 Old National including during all Damascus Road Pike, Mount Airy No Yes polling hours. Precinct 18-02 Yes Community Church 21771 18-02 voters will report to Linganore High School for the Primary and General. While Precinct 09-05 also votes at Linganore High School (operating from the Cafeteria), Precinct 18-02 will be clearly signed and operate from a separate room within the same school building. Election officials and signage will be present to direct all voters to their correct check-in stations. Frederick County - Precinct Reduction Info WHY IS DOES THE THERE NO PRECINCT POLLING DOES THIS HAVE BOTH PLACE TO PRECINCT BELOW AVG. SERVE THEM PUBLIC HAVE DENSE PERCENTAGE IN THE REGISTERED % ELECTION % EARLY TRANSPORTA CONCENTRAT OF VOTER PRECINCT? PRECINCT % IN PERSON % BY MAIL VOTERS IN DAY VOTING TION IONS OF TURNOUT HOW DOES 2024 v. 2025 OPTIONS REGISTERED AND AN THE COUNTY VOTERS? ABOVE AVG. PLAN TO WHERE? PERCENTAGE SERVE OF DIVERSE VOTERS IN RESIDENTS? THESE AREAS? GG22 - 36.86 GG22 - 9.99 GG22 - 27.56 GG22 - 7.43 No suitable 24 - 5320 25 - Yes, majority of 1002 PP24 - 11.70 PP24 - 7.02 PP24 - 9.37 PP24 - 1.87 Yes facility 5633 precinct. PG24 - 56.35 PG24 - 16.25 PG24 - 33.20 PG24 - 20.48 available. Consolidated precinct.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:03.515819+00:00"}
