{"chunk_id": "d405a6f0-afbb-4351-84ba-f1d72ff206fe", "source_url": "local://2026-01/Election Plan Board Presentation part 3.pdf", "title": "Election Plan Board Presentation part 3", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-01"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 13, "word_count": 211, "text": "PART 3 2 0 2 6 E l e c t i o n P l a n Early Voting Centers, Ballot Drop Boxes, and Polling Place Plans PART 3 L o cal B oar d s of E le ct ions I n cl u d e d i n t h is R ep or t : Anne Arundel County (Polling Place Plans) (part 2) Baltimore City (included-partial) Baltimore County (part 2) Frederick County (part 1) Prince George's County (part 1) ELECTION PLAN REQUIREMENTS Purpose: In 2025, HB0274 was passed which changed the process of approving early voting centers, ballot drop boxes, and polling plans. Previously, each section was submitted and approved individually. Now, all three sections are presented together for approval. This report includes all three sections under the guidance of the following regulations*: Election Plan, General: ▫ 33.01.08.01- 04 General Provisions, Election Plan Early Voting Centers: ▫ 33.17.02.02 Early Voting, Early Voting Centers, Selecting Early Voting Centers Ballot Drop Boxes: ▫ 33.11.01.04 Absentee Ballots, Definitions; General Provisions; Ballot Drop Boxes Polling Place Plans: ▫ 33.15.03.01 Polling Places, Required Plan ▫ 33.15.03.02 Polling Places, New or Changed Polling Place *links to DSD website where the most updated version of COMAR can be searched for the above listed regulations.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:05.551590+00:00"}
