{"chunk_id": "be3512c2-abb9-4689-a8d1-9013268ad719", "source_url": "local://2026-02/Election Plan 02 Presentation.pdf", "title": "Election Plan 02 Presentation", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-02"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 33, "chunk_total": 63, "word_count": 281, "text": "LBE’s analysis properly showed no negative effect on access to voting for historically disenfranchised communities. Baltimore City - Minority Population Map Baltimore City - Income Map Baltimore City - Voter Turnout Map Recommendation: Approve P r i n c e G e o r g e ' s POLLING PLACE PLANS 2022 2024 2026 Number of 228 228 223 Individual Buildings Number of 327 327 327 Precincts Number of 240 240 236 Polling Places Presiden t Substitute Members Beatrice P. Tignor Michael M. Gorman Carlett a L. Lundy Vice President LaVerne Poteat Scott Roberta B. Deegan Elections Administrator Member s Wendy N. Honesty-Bey Faye M. H owell Felicia N. Pratt Counsel Terri L. Williams Arthur J. Horne, Jr., Esq. Prince George’s County Board of Elections 1100 Mercantile Lane, Suite 115A Largo, Maryland 20774 Office: 301-341-7300 Fax: 301-341-7391 http://elections.mypgc.us election@co.pg.md.us TO: Jared DeMarinis FROM: Wendy N. Honesty-Bey WNHB Date: February 10, 2026 RE: Polling Place/Building Totals Discrepancy Prince George’s County Board of Elections (PGCBOE) is writing to formally notify the State Board of Elections (SBE) of corrections to the Polling Place Plan (PPP) previously submitted for approval. Upon further review, PGCBOE identified errors in the total number of polling places and buildings included in the submission. The information previously submitted indicated 238 polling places and 228 buildings. The correct totals are 236 polling places and 223 buildings. These errors occurred due to reporting issues with our internal Polling Place Master List Smartsheet. Specifically, two combined polling place sites remained listed as individual polling places and were inadvertently included in the overall totals. As a result, they were incorrectly counted as separate polling places when they should have been removed from the count.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:22.071920+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "feb123cb-d441-4811-93a2-18f0251d7196", "source_url": "local://2026-02/Election Plan 02 Presentation.pdf", "title": "Election Plan 02 Presentation", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-02"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 34, "chunk_total": 63, "word_count": 271, "text": "These errors occurred due to reporting issues with our internal Polling Place Master List Smartsheet. Specifically, two combined polling place sites remained listed as individual polling places and were inadvertently included in the overall totals. As a result, they were incorrectly counted as separate polling places when they should have been removed from the count. Due to the volume of polling place adjustments required to accommodate facilities that were temporarily or no longer available, the reduction in the total number of buildings was inadvertently overlooked during the consolidation process. PGCBOE confirms that: • There are no changes to voter precinct assignments resulting from the numerical corrections noted above. • The reduction in the number of buildings reflects previously implemented consolidations and does not represent new or additional changes beyond those already incorporated into the Polling Place Plan. Additionally, while reviewing the Google Sheet sent to me on Tuesday, February 12, 2026, we also found discrepancies withing the spreadsheet. Several polling place locations listed do not match those submitted by PGCBOE, and some locations appearing in the spreadsheet lack a corresponding Polling Place Plans submitted to SBE. The following five (5) polling places require correction to ensure alignment between the spreadsheet and the official Polling Place Plan submission: 1. 03-003 Listed as St. Mary of the Assumption Catholic School (listed on Google Sheet, but has since been corrected) Should be: Upper Marlboro Community Center, 5400 Marlboro Race Track RD, Upper Marlboro, MD (Polling Place Plan was submitted with this information) 2. 06-011 Listed as District Heights Family & Youth Servs (listed on Google Sheet, but has since been corrected) Should be: E.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:22.071931+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "d39a0b9e-4e6c-428f-bea1-90aa1c2154a8", "source_url": "local://2026-02/Election Plan 02 Presentation.pdf", "title": "Election Plan 02 Presentation", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-02"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 35, "chunk_total": 63, "word_count": 278, "text": "Mary of the Assumption Catholic School (listed on Google Sheet, but has since been corrected) Should be: Upper Marlboro Community Center, 5400 Marlboro Race Track RD, Upper Marlboro, MD (Polling Place Plan was submitted with this information) 2. 06-011 Listed as District Heights Family & Youth Servs (listed on Google Sheet, but has since been corrected) Should be: E. Michael Roll Municipal BlDG, 2000 Marbury Dr., District Heights, MD (Polling Place Plan was submitted with this information) 3. 06-14/06-029 Listed as Temple Hills Community Center (Listed on Google Sheet, but has since been corrected) Should be: Samuel Chase Elem SCH, 5700 Fisher RD, Temple Hills, MD 4. 20-005 Listed as Robert Frost Elem SCH (Listed on Google Sheet) Should be: Charles Carroll Middle School, 6130 Lamont Drive, New Carrollton, MD 5. 21-002 Listed as Univ. of MD Ritchie Coliseum (List on Google Sheet) Should be: College Park City Hall – Community Room, 7401 Baltimore Ave, College Park, MD PGCBOE regrets the oversight and appreciates the State Board’s understanding as we work together to ensure accuracy. Please let us know if any additional documentation or action is needed to support this correction. Prince George’s - 2026 Precinct and Polling Place map Prince George’s - 2026 Polling Locations PRECINCT LOCATED SUITABLE POLLING WHERE POLLING NEAR ADA PUBLIC BUILDING PRECINCT ADDRESS FOR PLACE IN POLLING PLACE MAJORITY COMPLIANT BUILDING TYPE ELECTION PRECINCT PLACE IS OF VOTERS LOCATED CALVERTON 3400 1001 ELEMENTARY BELTSVILLE Yes Yes Yes Yes School Yes SCHOOL ROAD BELTSVILLE 3900 Community 1002 COMMUNITY SELLMAN Yes Yes Yes Yes No 01-05 Center CENTER ROAD HIGH POINT 3601 POWDER 1003 Yes Yes Yes Yes School Yes HIGH SCHOOL MILL ROAD M.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:22.071941+00:00"}
