{"chunk_id": "cae1af5a-8230-4e94-ba8d-6d227aa256f0", "source_url": "local://2026-02/Election Plan 02 Presentation.pdf", "title": "Election Plan 02 Presentation", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-02"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 62, "chunk_total": 63, "word_count": 32, "text": "LBE’s analysis properly showed no negative effect on access to voting for historically disenfranchised communities. Prince George’s - Minority Population Map Prince George’s - Income Map Prince George’s - Voter Turnout Map", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:22.072335+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "c8f0ed17-016d-4feb-a351-bc83b518de27", "source_url": "local://2026-02/MDGOP-LtrToJaredDeMarinis-260203.pdf", "title": "MDGOP-LtrToJaredDeMarinis-260203", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-02"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_total": 3, "word_count": 276, "text": "February 3, 2026 Jared DeMarinis State Administrator of Elections Maryland State Board of Elections 151 West Street, Suite 200 Annapolis, MD 21401 Dear Mr. DeMarinis, As requested, the Maryland Republican Party is submitting our comments and concerns regarding proposed changes to the challengers and watchers regulations. Following my comments here, I have included the comments from many members of our Republican County Central Committees for your review. As you will read, we have quite a few concerns and do not support the majority of the changes proposed. I believe that my County RCC members have covered most of the points well, so I will be brief in my breakdown. 01. A1. I understand why “an individual” may be too generic, but limiting it to “a registered Maryland voter” may be too limiting. I can see instances when an outside observer is warranted or needed. Some members are suggesting “a United States citizen” instead. 01. A2. I love training, but I do believe there should be options of in-person, online, or even reading on their own. 01. B1&2 The points made above apply here as well. 01. C1. Why are we limiting people’s involvement in our election process? We’re trying to make it harder and more complicated when it shouldn’t be. 01. D2. Again, we’re making it complicated and harder for people to be involved. We need more transparency and availability in the process, not less. 01. D4 This is a real concern for my county central committees. This is too limiting. As the minority party in this state, we are often recruiting people all the way up until election day. I AUTHORITY MARYLAND REPUBLICAN PARTY; R.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:23.298391+00:00"}
{"chunk_id": "3a108e4f-cc69-459c-96a7-b355626ab501", "source_url": "local://2026-02/MDGOP-LtrToJaredDeMarinis-260203.pdf", "title": "MDGOP-LtrToJaredDeMarinis-260203", "section_hierarchy": ["2026-02"], "page_classification": "local_document", "chunking_strategy": "local_pdf", "chunk_index": 1, "chunk_total": 3, "word_count": 244, "text": "We need more transparency and availability in the process, not less. 01. D4 This is a real concern for my county central committees. This is too limiting. As the minority party in this state, we are often recruiting people all the way up until election day. I AUTHORITY MARYLAND REPUBLICAN PARTY; R. CHRISTOPHER ROSENTHAL, TREASURER cannot tell you how many times in the last 10 years I have had people come to me at the very last minute and say they want to help. We need to be able to recruit and involve people up until the end of the election. 01. E This becomes burdensome not only for the County RCCs, but for the MDGOP. There will be times when someone gets sick or needs to be closer to home, and exchanges need to be made. Last-minute changes happen. This would require our paperwork to be prepared for any and all possible changes, which will be lengthy and complicated. Again, why are we discouraging people from participating and being less accessible? 02. C. (2) Absolutely opposed to changing “shall” to “may”. Words have legal definitions; this is a change the Maryland Republican Party cannot support. Thank you for your time and attention to our feedback. If you have any questions or concerns regarding the MDGOP’s point of view on the proposed changes, please feel free to reach out to discuss. Sincerely, Nicole Beus Harris Chairwoman Maryland Republican Party AUTHORITY MARYLAND REPUBLICAN PARTY; R.", "date_extracted": "2026-04-17T18:09:23.298459+00:00"}
